    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **70 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` feature on the owner response. `riskFlag` is `true` when any of three conditions hold, else `false`:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 the owner's stored `possibleDuplicate` flag (soft-match on soundex(lastName) + postcode).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2014 a new, weaker relation than the exact disposable-domain blocklist (exact matches are already rejected with 400 at creation, so they never reach a stored owner). A domain qualifies when it *is*, is a *subdomain of*, or *shares the second-level label of* a known disposable domain (e.g. `mail.mailinator.com` or `mailinator.org` for the blocked `mailinator.com`).\n3. **City over soft capacity** \u2014 the stored `capacityWarning` flag (city already held \u226540 owners, approaching the hard limit of 50).\n\n### Changes\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only boolean `riskFlag` property to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this at build time).\n- **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `riskFlag` backed by a derived `deriveRiskFlag(Owner)` method plus helpers for the disposable-adjacent check.\n\n### Notable gotcha resolved\nMy first pass declared the `isDisposableAdjacentEmail(String)` / `secondLevelLabel(String)` helpers as `default` interface methods. MapStruct treated the `String \u2192 String` `secondLevelLabel` as an automatic property-type converter and injected it into the *reverse* `toOwner(...)` mapping, causing NPEs (HTTP 500) on every create. Marking those helpers `private` removed them from MapStruct's candidate-method set while keeping them callable from `deriveRiskFlag`; `deriveRiskFlag` itself takes an `Owner` param, so it can't be mis-selected as a scalar converter.",
